RUN: not %COMPILE %S/first.st %S/second.st --error-format clang 2>&1 | %CHECK %s

Every file is parsed before the run aborts, so the errors of both files are reported, each once.
The abort that follows does not repeat them.
CHECK: {{.*}}first.st:4:{{[0-9]+}}:{{.*}}: error[E006]: Missing expected Token KeywordColon or KeywordComma
CHECK-NEXT: {{.*}}first.st:5:1:{{.*}}: error[E006]: Missing expected Token KeywordColon
CHECK-NEXT: {{.*}}first.st:5:1:{{.*}}: error[E007]: Unexpected token: expected DataTypeDefinition but found KeywordEndVar
CHECK-NEXT: {{.*}}first.st:5:1:{{.*}}: error[E006]: Missing expected Token [KeywordSemicolon]
CHECK-NEXT: {{.*}}first.st:5:1:{{.*}}: error[E007]: Unexpected token: expected KeywordSemicolon but found 'END_VAR'
CHECK-NEXT: {{.*}}second.st:2:{{[0-9]+}}:{{.*}}: error[E007]: Unexpected token: expected expression but found ;
CHECK-NEXT: error: Compilation aborted due to critical parse errors
CHECK-NOT: {{.*}} at: {{.*}}
